WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.050
- No one likes making their bed,

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.070
let alone washing their sheets.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.793
Especially single men.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.540
In one survey, 55% of
single men between 18 and 25

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.993
reported changing their
sheets only four times a year.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.770
And to be clear,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.603
those are beds that you
would not want to sleep in.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.640
You shed about 15 million
skin cells each night,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.260
but they don't just
pile up in your sheets.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.980
Because something else is already there

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.593
waiting to gobble them up:

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.060
dust mites.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.390
And the longer you wait between washes,

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.960
the more food these critters will have

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.710
and the more they'll
procreate and multiply.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.550
So if you don't wash your sheets,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.710
you'll be sleeping with hundreds
of thousands of arachnids.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.370
Now, for the estimated
20 million Americans

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.010
with dust allergies, it gets worse.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.120
Dust mites and their
feces produce proteins

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.760
that cause red and
itchy eyes, runny noses,

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.560
and other cold-like symptoms
in people who are allergic.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.360
And dust mites, well, they're actually not

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.313
the only allergen in a dirty bed.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.090
If you never wash your pillow sheets,

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.700
a community of fungus
can also build up there.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.940
One study found that a typical pillow

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.400
has as many as 16
different species of fungus

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.703
and literally millions of fungal spores.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.280
And the most common among them,

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.410
Aspergillus fumigatus,
is potentially dangerous.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.530
In addition to allergic reactions,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.390
it can infect your lungs and other organs.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.430
And it's not just fungi joining the party.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.782
You see, bacteria also love a good

00:01:45.782 --> 00:01:47.731
unwashed pillow case or sheet

00:01:47.731 --> 00:01:48.564
a lot.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.470
Another study found that
unwashed pillow cases and sheets

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:56.780
had up to 39 times more
bacteria than pet-food bowls

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.320
and several thousand times more
bacteria than a toilet seat.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.630
Like Staphylococcus aureus,

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.913
which in some rare cases can be deadly.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.230
Now on a slightly less or
perhaps more frightening note,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.003
dirty sheets can also give you acne.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.265
Each night, the oil, lotion,

00:02:18.265 --> 00:02:20.210
and other cosmetics on your skin

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.770
transfer to your sheets
and build up over time

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.280
until eventually your bedding is basically

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.323
a giant used makeup wipe.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.980
Then during the following nights,

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.320
all that gunk transfers
back onto your body,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.850
clogging your pores, and,
viola, you've got acne.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.120
Fortunately, there's a simple way

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.033
to avoid all of these problems:

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.743
Wash your sheets, and wash them often.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.060
Experts recommend about once a week

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.590
using the hottest water possible.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.850
That'll kill a lot of
bacteria and dust mites,

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.460
get out stains, and remove oils.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.870
Plus, as awful as making
your bed might be,

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.630
there's simply nothing better

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:07.501
than slipping between clean, crisp sheets.

